 "top_rows_text_sample": "Top-level acceptance: all child sub-requirements pass or link to an open register entry with active reconstruction.",
 "texts": {
  "TL": "Timeline row T1-001 (tier documented) has a visual realization or an open register entry.",
  "EP": "Epilogue row E-001 (PDF tier documented; sources are encyclopedia/blog leads, so verify before use) is realized or registered.",
  "SS": "State-schedule entry S-001 changes state at its documented window.",
  "WK": "Construction chronology entry E-01 is built on screen, never pre-placed.",
  "GE": "Gun emplacement G-01 carries gun type/count and prepared-vs-improvised state.",
  "PE": "Pre-existing feature P-01 is present at frame one, never animated as construction.",
  "CT": "Terrain source catalog item #1 has a status and is used or registered.",
  "CF": "Conflict C-001 (Meade reaches Gettysburg (Jul 1-2)) carries every value as a selectable scenario; default is an owner decision.",
  "OA": "Battle Theatre is a separate page/section with its own renderer, entry button and Back with no leaked WebGL/audio; read-only reuse of the 16 tour stops and 512 monuments as camera bookmarks."
 },
 "oa_texts": {
  "OA01.0000": "Battle Theatre is a separate page/section with its own renderer, entry button and Back with no leaked WebGL/audio; read-only reuse of the 16 tour stops and 512 monuments as camera bookmarks.",
  "OA02.0000": "Every soldier individually animated; total rendered equals the number present (PDF Section N agrees: one-to-one, no performance capping without a recorded owner decision).",
  "OA03.0000": "Complete roster section of both armies (names need not appear in the animation); source and rights per name. The PDF has no roster requirement.",
  "OA04.0000": "Rufus Dawes and all named commanders accurate in uniform, equipment and weapons; where no source exists the gap is registered per Law cl.3, not invented.",
  "OA05.0000": "Real period-accurate weapon audio per individual shot. CONFLICTS with PDF Section S / Q23 labeling: see DEC-001.",
  "OA06.0000": "Unit activity, orientation and position match the record: owner target well over 97%, measured on documented unit-level quantities.",
  "OA07.0000": "Hollywood-grade human movement incl. artillery fire and impact; no standard relaxed silently; shortfalls reported.",
  "OA08.0000": "Every event from first shot to withdrawal is on the timeline and playable.",
  "OA09.0000": "Main-map background is a source-traced July 1863 reconstruction (B.9 pipeline); the site uses only actual Gettysburg images.",
  "OA10.0000": "Owner chat 2026-11-13: the finished Battle Theatre has an accurate 3D representation of the entire battlefield as it was during the battle: renders of the town, the buildings, the terrain and any kind of structure (the owner's wording is '100% accurate'; the claim made to users stays governed by Law cl.3 and DEC-003: strongest evidence-based reconstruction, tier-marked, gaps registered).",
  "OA11.0000": "Owner chat 2026-11-13: soldiers are shown doing the work and the routine of the armies: building artillery positions, earthworks and defenses, and ordinary things such as eating meals in their camps.",
  "OA12.0000": "Owner chat 2026-11-13: accurate renders of field hospitals, including accurate battle trauma and period-accurate treatment methods."
 },
